# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first stage does `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is shipped to the
# daemon and cached in the builder layers — even though the runtime stage copies
# only `.next/standalone`, `.next/static`, `public/` and `backend/`.
#
# Keep this in step with `.gitignore`. The two entries that matter most are
# `refworld/` and `refs/`: the first is a real world save containing real Steam
# IDs and player names, and neither has any business in a build context.

# ─── Never build-context these ───
refworld/
refs/
# Exported conversation transcripts (see .gitignore).
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.txt

# ─── Secrets ───
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Rebuilt inside the image ───
node_modules
.next
.venv
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ─── Not needed at runtime ───
.git
.github
.gitignore
*.md
docs/
backend/tests/
pytest.ini
vitest.config.ts
eslint.config.mjs
scripts/setup-dev.sh

# ─── Local state ───
cache/
backups/
*.db
*.sqlite3
